# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# Two deployment modes — pick one:
#
# 1) LOCAL (private, free): all generation stays on this machine via Ollama.
#    Requires: ollama serve + `ollama pull gpt-oss:20b`
ARCHWOVEN_MODE=local
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
# Overall native inference budget, including repairs (default 180 seconds).
# ARCHWOVEN_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
# Job execution budget starts after the concurrency queue (default 180 seconds).
# ARCHWOVEN_JOB_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
#
# 2) HOSTED: generation calls the Anthropic API.
#    Comment out ARCHWOVEN_MODE above and set your key:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-…
# Server-selected model; restart after changing. Opus remains the default.
# ARCHWOVEN_HOSTED_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# Also supported for evaluation: claude-sonnet-5-5, claude-haiku-5-5.
#
# Shared hosted jobs and spending limits (Upstash REST): configure all four.
# For local testing use a dedicated prefix; Vercel Preview and Production also
# need separate prefixes. Each prefix needs an explicitly initialized spending
# ledger; their combined caps must stay inside your approved budget.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-database.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# ARCHWOVEN_REDIS_PREFIX=archwoven-dev:
# Stable, cryptographically random secret of at least 32 characters. Keep it
# server-side; changing it invalidates visitor sessions and job ownership.
# ARCHWOVEN_SESSION_SECRET=
# Never prefix these variables with NEXT_PUBLIC_. On Vercel, set them in the
# project's environment settings rather than committing an env file.
# From the repository root, inspect the ledger without making a provider call:
# node --env-file=apps/web/.env.local scripts/spending-ledger.mjs status
# See README "Hosted spending limits" to initialize the ledger once.
#
# Optional local evaluation cap: explicitly initialize a SEPARATE ledger first
# with `pnpm eval:budget init /absolute/path/evaluation-budget.db <approved-usd>`.
# Keep the same file across restarts/models. Never configure this on Vercel.
# ARCHWOVEN_EVAL_BUDGET_DB=/absolute/path/evaluation-budget.db
